{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792943681,"nonce":"c8paLOCtTJDJI15BfPBkPP+pCCc=","message":"Decisions (darmie, 2026-10-25): the session owns the terminal, project builds and runs, so the language server and everything that builds or runs the project start in the session; the page is the editor UI. The Rayzor language server does not need cranelift or llvm for inference, so a frontend-only build leaves both out (this is the `frontend` feature on the compiler crate, with the 22 runtime constants moved to rayzor-runtime-core and cranelift_backend/tiered_backend gated).\n\nMeasured: RayDE as it is today (`haxe -D wasm -D ashui_window -dce full -main rayde.Main`, then `ASH_WASM_FIBERS=1 ash --build --target wasm32-wasip1-threads`): rayde.hl is 4.5 MB; 7661 of 7661 functions lower, none refused; the module is 33.6 MB uncompressed with fibers on (ashui's dashboard is 23.0 MB for 3,095 functions). The HDLLs it names (rayscript, cterm) have no side module yet, so a primitive from them raises when reached. Not yet run in a page. Compression and a smaller dce set are the first levers; the native-backed features move to the session.","files":null}]}